## 10.6 sparklines: gtExtras method
Before we can prepare the sales report by product by using gtExtras functions, code chunk below will be used to prepare the data.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="true"}
report <- coffeechain %>%
  mutate(Year = year(Date)) %>%
  filter(Year == "2013") %>%
  mutate (Month = month(Date, 
                        label = TRUE, 
                        abbr = TRUE)) %>%
  group_by(Product, Month) %>%
  summarise(Sales = sum(Sales)) %>%
  ungroup()
```
:::


It is important to note that one of the requirement of gtExtras functions is that almost exclusively is required to pass data.frame with list columns. In view of this, code chunk below will be used to convert the report data.frame into list columns.

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="true"}
report %>%
  group_by(Product) %>%
  summarize('Monthly Sales' = list(Sales), 
            .groups = "drop")
```

